---
name: handoff
description: Saves or loads a Claude Code session handoff. Use `/handoff --save [instruction]` to save the current session and `/handoff` to list saved handoffs. Load a saved handoff by its list number.
argument-hint: "[--save instruction | N]"
disable-model-invocation: true
allowed-tools: Bash(python3 __SKILL_DIR__/handoff.py:*)
---

!`python3 __SKILL_DIR__/handoff.py load --self ${CLAUDE_SESSION_ID} -- $ARGUMENTS`

The block above contains the local handoff script output.

- If it starts with `HANDOFF SAVED BY SKILL`, relay the message in one or two sentences and mention that the hook did not intercept the command. Do nothing else.
- If it starts with `NO SAVED HANDOFFS` or `SAVED HANDOFFS`, relay it without changes or commentary. Do not run tools.
- If it starts with `HANDOFF` or `WARNING`, it is context from the session being continued. Read the transcript or files only when the current task needs them. Always reply in the language the user used in that session.
  - If it contains `Continuation instruction`, execute that instruction immediately as if the user had just sent it.
  - Otherwise, summarize the previous session in 2–4 sentences and wait for the next instruction.
